{
    "type": "Collection",
    "id": "PACE_OCI_L3B_CLOSE_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The Closed-Loop Ocean Simulation for Evaluation of ocean color retrieval algorithms (CLOSE) Level-3 binned collection provides spatially aggregated ocean-color products generated from the CLOSE Level-2 observations using an equal-area global binning structure. Products include hyperspectral remote sensing reflectance, chlorophyll-a concentration, diffuse attenuation coefficients, aerosol optical properties, and derived absorption and backscattering properties. These data support statistical analysis, evaluation of spatial aggregation effects, and generation of Level-3 mapped products.\n\n Geophysical variables in this suite include:\n  - Rrs_346 through Rrs_719 \u2014 Hyperspectral remote sensing reflectance at OCI wavelengths (sr\u207b\u00b9)\n  - chlor_a \u2014 Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg m\u207b\u00b3)\n  - Kd \u2014 Diffuse attenuation coefficients (m\u207b\u00b9)\n  - a \u2014 Total absorption (m\u207b\u00b9)\n  - adg \u2014 Absorption due to colored dissolved and detrital material (m\u207b\u00b9)\n  - aph \u2014 Absorption due to phytoplankton (m\u207b\u00b9)\n  - bb \u2014 Total backscattering (m\u207b\u00b9)\n  - bbp \u2014 Particulate backscattering (m\u207b\u00b9)\n  - angstrom \u2014 Aerosol \u00c5ngstr\u00f6m exponent\n  - aot_865 \u2014 Aerosol optical thickness at 865 nm\n  - BinIndex and BinList \u2014 Level-3 bin indexing and observation-assignment information",
